{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-18T20:00:11.476Z","data":{"text":"Done. Summary of the work on task 2:\n\n**Implemented**\n- `validate_delta` in `src/validate/delta.rs`: `unknown-delta-section`, `empty-delta-section`, `missing-delta-sections`, `requirement-outside-section`, `unpaired-rename`, `invalid-rename`, `duplicate-requirement`, `conflicting-delta`, plus requirement validation for ADDED/MODIFIED.\n- `check_delta_targets` in `src/validate/delta_targets.rs`: `unknown-requirement` for MODIFIED, REMOVED and RENAMED FROM entries, with the RENAMED-TO exception.\n- `validate_change` in `src/validate/change.rs`: per-delta validation against the living spec, folder byte order, `change-without-delta`, and read errors.\n- A line-accurate delta scan in `src/validate/delta_scan.rs` that reuses `outline::scan` and the parse's own `split_sections`/`rename_side`/`is_invalid_rename`/`removed_bullet_name` helpers (made `pub(crate)`).\n- Entry, duplicate and conflict rules in `src/validate/delta_entries.rs`.\n- Re-exports in `lib.rs`; tests in `tests/validating_deltas.rs` and `tests/validating_deltas_rules.rs`.\n\n**Verification**\n- `cargo test -p osq-kernel-specs --test validating_deltas` green.\n- `sh scripts/verify-rust.sh` exits 0 (fmt, clippy `-D warnings`, all tests incl. corpus).\n- cargo-mutants over every touched source file: no missed mutants, no timeouts.\n- All files ≤250 lines, functions ≤80; task 1's tests pass unchanged.\n\nThe one notable deviation (documented in the result): the delta scan went into `delta_scan.rs` rather than `outline.rs`, because extending `outline.rs` pushed it over the 250-line cap; `outline.rs` is left exactly as task 1 wrote it.\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/217-rust-specs-validate/.run/results/2.md`."}}
